    "id": "v2-4fd080-p4-midpoint-slot-1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the coordinates of point $P$ that divides $A(6,-5)$ and $B(-2,3)$ in the ratio $3:5$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(3,-2)$\n\nMove three eighths of each coordinate difference from A towards B.",
      "worked": "$P$ is three eighths of the distance from $A$ to $B$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x_P &= 6+\\frac{3}{8}\\bigl(-2-6\\bigr)\\\\x_P &= 3\\\\y_P &= -5+\\frac{3}{8}\\bigl(3-(-5)\\bigr)\\\\y_P &= -2\\end{align*}$$\n$P(3,-2)$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
